
// A colored shape transported through TWO nested remaps: a reflection in x, then
// a translation. Its color must compose BOTH — sampling ball.color at
// reflect(p - offset) = [4 - p.x, p.y, p.z] — not just the inner reflect. Guards
// the nested-remap flatten in the color resolver (flattenRemaps): the
// compositional resolver emits nested inline remaps, and the backend drops a
// nested remap's OUTER coordinate unless they are composed first. A single-remap
// program (color_remap.gsl) has an identity outer coordinate, so it can't catch
// this — the dropped coordinate there is harmless.
ball = sphere(1);
ball.color = [clamp(p.x, 0, 1), 0, 0];

reflected = remap(ball, [-p.x, p.y, p.z]);
moved = remap(reflected, p - [4, 0, 0]);
return moved;
